  "_about": "Seconds Stryker spends on each mutation piece; mutation.mjs deals the shards by them. Fitted by least squares to the 36 measured shard times of runs 45157220742 and 45160742243 (worker threads, 5 s test limit): a piece costs 0.0074 s per test run against its mutants, 9.51 s per mutant that timed out and 0.30 s per mutant, its counts the mean of the two runs' reports. Timeouts are what made shard 8 slow: src/tools/facilities.ts:61-71 is a static table whose mutants run the whole suite and 63 of them timed out. src/tools/handlers.ts's pieces moved in the get_departures, check_road_status and check_weather_warnings parity fix: a piece with the same source text as a measured one keeps its seconds; a moved, changed or new piece shares the seconds of the file's old pieces it replaces (those not matched by text) pro-rata by syntax weight — carried by text, re-measured at the next release run. The parking, location, POI, weather, autobahn and address parity fix moved handlers.ts's, location.ts's and validate.ts's pieces and added parking-words.ts, osm-words.ts, weather-block.ts and address-words.ts: carried the same way, a new file's pieces at the scope's mean seconds per syntax weight. The mock-parity branch (the API's answers in today's words) changed client.ts, types.ts, presentation.ts, context.ts, handlers.ts, fuel.ts, facilities.ts, find-place.ts, location.ts, nearby.ts, trains.ts, transit.ts, watch-words.ts, weather-block.ts and address-words.ts, and added departure-words.ts, departures-input.ts, flix-words.ts, fuel-words.ts, road-forecast.ts, road-status-words.ts, station-sections.ts and transit-words.ts: every seconds value of those files' moved, changed or new pieces is an ESTIMATE carried as above (a new piece at the scope's mean seconds per syntax weight, or set by hand where nothing matched), never measured; the next release run measures them. The move to API 1.2.1 (the place resolver, the stop boards and the station page released) moved pieces of types.ts, handlers.ts and station-sections.ts: carried the same way, by source text and pro-rata by syntax weight from the file's replaced pieces, so those seconds are ESTIMATES too until the next release run measures them. src/tools/osm-words.ts held its words in module-level tables, static to Stryker: each of the ~1,000 mutants ran the whole suite (~955 tests), so the table's 259 s estimate stood for about two hours and held the 2.7.4 and 2.7.5 release runs' shard 6 past its 20-minute limit. The tables are built in functions now (per-test coverage, about one test a mutant), and the file's three pieces are MEASURED: one local Stryker run of those pieces, each weighed by this fit from its report (0.30 s a mutant, 0.0074 s a test run, 9.51 s a timeout). src/log-mask.ts held its patterns and quote pairs in module-level constants, static to Stryker (139 static mutants, the run's shard 13 at 17 min 10 s against 554 s dealt); they are built in functions now and the file's pieces are MEASURED the same way (a local Stryker run of its pieces, weighed by this fit). src/tools/place-words.ts's table was static the same way (103 static mutants, 59 timeouts); it is built in a function now and its pieces are MEASURED the same way. src/tools/facilities.ts's glossary (the static table of 2.7.2's 63 timeouts) and its state words are built in functions now and its pieces are MEASURED the same way. src/tools/find-place.ts's kind, Land and Kreis tables were static the same way (88 static mutants, 59 timeouts); built in functions now, its pieces MEASURED the same way. src/tools/region.ts's Länder table was static the same way (66 static mutants, 24 timeouts); built in a function now, its pieces MEASURED the same way. src/tools/station-page.ts's Länder and kind order were static the same way (49 static mutants at 34-43); built in functions now, its pieces MEASURED the same way.",
